{"answer":"It sounds like you're ready to level up your slow cooker game! Here are some key tips to get better results:\n\n1. **Don't peek**: Every time you lift the lid, you release heat and add 20-30 minutes of cooking time. Trust the process and keep the lid on.\n2. **Brown meat first**: Searing beef or chicken before adding it to the slow cooker adds deep flavor and improves texture.\n3. **Layer wisely**: Put root vegetables (potatoes, carrots) at the bottom, then meat, then liquids—since veggies cook slower.\n4. **Cut ingredients evenly**: Uniform sizes ensure everything cooks at the same rate.\n5. **Don't overfill**: Fill the slow cooker ½ to ¾ full for even cooking. Too full = undercooked; too empty = overcooked.\n6. **Use less liquid than you think**: Slow cookers trap steam, so you need less liquid than stovetop recipes. Excess liquid makes things watery.\n7. **Add dairy and herbs late**: Milk, cream, and fresh herbs break down or lose flavor if cooked too long. Stir them in during the last 30 minutes.\n8. **Adjust seasoning at the end**: Flavors mellow during long cooking,","answer_attempts":1,"answer_latency_seconds":3.698199,"answer_usage":{"completion_tokens":256,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":4708,"prompt_tokens":4708,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"total_tokens":4964},"arm":"oracle_context","estimated_cost_usd":0.00129316,"judge":"yes","judge_attempts":1,"judge_label":true,"judge_prompt_sha256":"7cc2aeb23ea39589b9fcfe9a4ae10157f6c49d7c73e6ac82932407a90a954c9f","judge_returned_model":"deepseek-v4-flash","judge_usage":{"completion_tokens":1,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":399,"prompt_tokens":399,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"total_tokens":400},"prompt_sha256":"448df7af3ed37ab739cfa4b092ea65562f11cc4f01b2906e8b646b671824c112","question_id":"caf03d32","question_type":"single-session-preference","returned_model":"deepseek-v4-flash","selected_session_ids":["answer_2fc6aabb"]}
